    "turn_text": "Yeah, I do. There's a great book just written by Tom Friedman called Thank You for Being Late. It's an Optimus Guide to America in the Age of Acceleration. He talks about all of this, and it's very interesting how quickly information passes and really serves as a basis from which to promote social change. But he said when he took over as New York Times columnist for James Rustin, who was a famed New York Times columnist, He said he used to go to work in the morning, and Rusta needs to say, I wonder what my seven other competitors throughout the country are writing. The other writers for the big papers, Mary McGrory and several others, Friedman says he now comes into his",
