    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "including right here, and you've been a leading figure in that effort with respect to the Buffalo Naga Medical Campus. Buffalo in America is a nation of immigrants. Ronald Reagan used to say that we don't care what your origins are, we care what your destination is. And that should be the prevailing ethos of Buffalo and America. We have great organizations like Jewish Family Services, like Journey Zen, like the International Institute, and so many others, that Catholic Charities, that knows how to do this stuff. We've taken generation of immigrants that have come here seeking their piece of the miracle that's America. And why would we stop that? It provides energy. It provides new ideas. Look at all the ethnic groups in Buffalo. But this is not new to our nation and our community. Back in the middle of the 19th century, there was a political party called the No Nothing Party. It was really the Native American Party, and they opposed. immigration to the United States from Europe. There's stated reason for opposing that was it didn't want the pope to run the American democracy. And that was their concern. The real concern was jobs. It's the same thing that you have going on here. And, you know, there's always when you feel grieved in your life, there's two things that you want to know. One is that the solution is easy and it's not your fault. And that's why minority groups and immigrants get scapegoated because it's easy and people fall into that and weak people that are frustrated are very vulnerable. You know, here's what I take major issue with the new president. The president of the United States is the leader of the free world. And when the nation is threatened, as it was in 9-11, it's the responsibility of the leader of the free world to marshal the resources of the federal government to say, look, we got this. We are going to make sure that you and your family are safe because what terrorists seek to do is disrupt your way of life. And this president creates a fake threat with a fake travel ban to create a fake sense of security. I don't know what's worse or more egregious. Is it the scapegoating of an immigrant group that there's no evidence that anybody from any of these countries ever came to our country and killed anybody or giving people a false sense of security? But the point is leadership is about taking people over the horizon. And when you spend as much as you do, we spend $600 billion a year on defense that you can't marshal the resources to say, don't worry about this. That's our responsibility. If you have something to worry about, we will tell you what you need to do in order to protect you and your family. But to create A false sense of threat is something entirely different than I've not seen. And America is better than this. We never scared that easily. We never scared that easily. And we shouldn't now and we shouldn't move into the future.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
